From 7fd2c95c387f24cc5ec254eafcaa1390dc9c44d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JingMatrix <jingmatrix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 14:04:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/47] Implement patch mode and per-level attestation identity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The per-profile operation mode gained a config field earlier; wire it through
and act on it in the router.

Patch mode (the default) forwards generateKey to the real HAL, keeps the real
hardware key blob untouched, and re-signs only the attestation leaf under the
keybox with the root of trust patched to locked/Verified. The key stays
hardware-backed and its authentic KeyMint attestation content survives; only the
root of trust and signing root change. The re-sign lives in the TA
(teesim_km_patch_attestation / resign.rs): x509-cert rebuilds the leaf and a small
DER splice replaces the RootOfTrust under its high-number [704] context tag, signed
by the same BoringSSL backend and keybox key generation uses. Generation stays the
fallback and PatchAttest falls back to it when the real HAL declines.

A level needs working hardware to patch: keystore2 resolves separate TEE and
StrongBox KeyMint proxies (both hooked), and a broken StrongBox — offered but unable
to attest, as on an unlocked dev unit — forces generation at that level via a
harvested strongBoxAvailable flag.

The record's security level and KeyMint version now follow the requesting HAL. One
TA serves both proxies, so before each creation the router passes the proxy's level
and the TA overrides hw_info.security_level and aidl_version for that one request,
restoring them after. Both versions are harvested from throwaway keys at each level;
a broken StrongBox reuses the TEE version. The aidl_version getter/setter is added to
kmr-ta via the seclevel patch.
